# Component organization (minimal)

Keep component rules short and practical. Favor existing patterns in nearby files.

## Placement

- Reusable primitives in `app/components/ui/`.
- Admin back-office UI in `app/components/admin/`.
- Shared auth chrome in `app/components/auth/`.
- Shared cross-surface components in `app/components/` (e.g. `slot-blocks.jsx`).
- **Storefront page UI** in `app/themes/<name>/components/` (not `app/components/`).
- Keep route-level data loading/mutations in routes and `app/core`, not in shared UI primitives.

## Boundaries

- `ui` components should be presentation-focused and reusable.
- Feature components can compose UI components and local hooks.
- Move business workflows to `app/core` when logic grows beyond view orchestration.
- Theme components receive data via props/loaders; do not import `app/core/*.server` modules from theme code.

## Naming and imports

- Component file names are lowercase and hyphenated.
- Use PascalCase for component function names.
- In `app/components/`, use `#/*` imports without file extensions.
- In `app/themes/<slug>/`, import sibling theme modules with relative paths; keep `#/…` for core app modules (`#/core`, `#/components`, `#/libs`, etc.).
- Document component props with JSDoc (`@param {Object} props` + per-prop lines) — follow `app/components/admin/` patterns; see [jsdoc-types.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/jsdoc-types.mdc).
